[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:61. Trouble with the Hubble]
[00:00.620]Passage 61 | 文章六十一
[00:02.830]Dangerous descent. | 危险的下降。
[00:06.415]In future, astronauts will be required to descend from a spaceship, | 将来，宇航员将被要求从宇宙飞船上降落，
[00:12.555]while it is still in space, and to return to it. | 当飞船仍在太空中时，并返回飞船。
[00:16.570]The ability to do this will be necessary in future flights to distant planets. | 这种能力在未来前往遥远行星的飞行中是必要的。
[00:22.910]Scientists are now trying to discover if this is possible. | 科学家们现在正试图发现这是否可能。
[00:28.105]The spaceship Astra, | 宇宙飞船“阿斯特拉”，
[00:30.855]which left the earth a short time ago, | 不久前离开地球，
[00:33.650]will be travelling 300 miles into space. | 将飞向太空 300 英里。
[00:38.215]At a certain point, | 在某个特定点，
[00:40.940]the Astra will stop for a short time, | “阿斯特拉”号将短暂停留，
[00:44.270]and an astronaut will attempt to leave the stationary spaceship | 一名宇航员将尝试离开静止的飞船，
[00:48.960]and then return to it. | 然后返回飞船。
[00:51.615]We shall not know whether the experiment has been successful | 我们将不知道实验是否成功，
[00:56.070]until we have received a radio message. | 直到我们收到无线电信息。
[00:59.595]The first message is expected to arrive | 第一条信息预计将在
[01:02.860]at 7 o'clock this evening. | 今晚 7 点到达。
[01:05.465]By that time, the Astra will have been flying through space | 到那时，“阿斯特拉”号将已经在太空中飞行
[01:10.110]for 17 hours and will have circled the earth a great many times. | 17 小时，并已绕地球很多次。
[01:16.135]When the first radio messages have been received, | 当收到第一批无线电信息后，
[01:20.200]the results of the trip will be announced immediately. | 这次旅行的结果将立即公布。